hadiths[54]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2036","Qatadah bin An-Nu'man narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""When Allah loves a slave, He prevents him from the world, just as one of you prevents his sick from water."" Another chain reports a similar narration"
"2037","Usamah bin Sharik said:\Some Bedouins asked: 'O Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) shall we treat (our ill)?' He said: 'Yes"""
"2038","Aishah narrated:\Whenever one of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) became (feverishly) ill"""
"2039","Uqbah bin Amir Al-Juhani narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Do not force your sick to eat"""
"2040","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Use this black seed. For indeed it contains a cure for every disease except As-Sam\"" And As-Sam is death"""
"2041","Anas narrated \Some people from Urainah arrived in Al-Madinah"""
"2042","Abu Hurairah narrated (from the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w)):\Whoever kills himself with (an instrument of)iron"""
"2043","Abu Hurairah narrated (that the the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w)) said:\Whoever kills himself with (an instrument of)iron"""
"2044","Abu Hurairah narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) forbade from cures that are Khabith.\"" [Abu 'Elsa said:] Meaning poison"""
"2045","Simak narrated that he heard 'Alqamah bin Wa'il narrate from his father"
"2046","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Indeed the best of what you treat is As-Sa'ut"""
"2047","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Indeed the best of what you treat is As-Sa'ut"""
"2048","Imran bin Husain narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) prohibited cauterization. He said:\We were tested (with severe medical condition) so we were cauterized"""
"2049","Anas narrated:\The Prophet (S.A.W) cauterized As'ad bin Zurarah for Shawkah"""
"2050","Anas narrated:\The Prophet (S.A.W) would get cupped in his jugular veins and his upper back. And he would get cupped on the seventeenth (of the month)"""
"2051","Ibn Mas'ud said:\The Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) narrated about the Night of Isra'"""
"2052","Abbad bin Mansur narrated from 'Ikrimah who said:\Ibn 'Abbas had three boys who were cuppers. He would use the proceeds from two of them for himself and his family"""
"2053","Ali bin 'Ubaidullah narrated that his grandmother [Salma] - who used to serve the The Prophet (S.A.W) said:\There was no wound nor cut on the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) but he would order me to put Hinna on it.\"" Another chain reports a similar narration"""
"2054","Aqqar bin Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah narrated from his father who said that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Whoever seeks treatment by cauterization"""
"2055","Anas narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) permitted Ruqyah for the scorpion sting"
"2056","Imran bin Husain narrated that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said:\No Ruqyah except for the (evil) eye and the scorpion sting"""
"2057","Abu Sa'eed narrated:\The Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) would seek refuge from the jinn and the (evil) eye of humans"""
"2058","Asma' bint 'Umaish said:\ I said: 'O Messenger of Allah (S.A.W)! Some of Ja'far's children have suffered from an accelerated case of the inflammation of the eye"""
"2059","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) used to seek refuge for Al-Hasan and Al-Husain saying:\\""U'idhukuma bikalimatillahi-tammati"""
"2060","Hayyah bin Habis At-Tamimi narrated:My father narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) saying: \There is nothing to Al-Ham"""
"2061","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\If there was anything that could overcome the Decree then the (evil) eye would overcome it"""
"2062","Abu Sa'eed narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) dispatched us on a military expedition. We camped with some people and asked them to entertain us but they did not entertain us. Their leader was stung so they came to us saying: 'Is there anyone among you who can treat a scorpion sting with Ruqyah?' I said: 'Yes I can. But I will not do any Ruqyah until you give us some sheep.' They said: 'Then we shall give you thirty sheep.' We accepted that"""
"2063","Abu Sa'eed Al Khudri narrated:\Some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) came across a tribe of Bedouins that did not entertain them"""
"2064","Abu Khizamah narrated from his father who said:\I asked the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W): 'O Messenger of Allah(S.A.W)! Do you think that the Ruqyah we use"""
"2065","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said:\Al-'Ajwah is from Paradise and it contains a cure for poison. Truffles are a form of manna"""
"2066","Sa'eed bin Zaid narrated that the Prophet (S.A.W) said:\Truffles are a form of manna"""
"2067","Abu Hurairah narrated that people among the Companions of the Prophet (S.A.W) would say:\Truffles are the earth's smallpox.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said: \""Truffles are a form of manna"""
"2068","Qatadah said:\It was narrated to me that Abu Hurairah said: 'I took three truffles"""
"2069","Qatadah said:\It was narrated to me that Abu Hurairah said:'Ash-Shuniz is a cure for every disease except As-Sam.' Qatadah said: \""One takes twenty-one seeds daily"""
"2070","Abu Masud Al-Ansari narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) prohibited the price of a dog"""
"2071","Eisa Ibn 'Abdur-Raman bin Abi Laila said:\I entered upon 'Abdullah bin 'Ukaim Abu Mabad Al-Juhani to visit him"""
"2072","Rafi' bin Khadij narrated that the Prophet (S.A.W) said:\Fever is from the agitation of the Fire"""
"2073","Aishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said:\Fever is from the heat of the Hell"""
"2074","**Bundār, Aḥmad ibn Manīʿ, and Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān** narrated to us, they said: **Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī** narrated to us, from **Sufyān**, from **Abū Isḥāq**, from **Abū al-Aḥwaṣ**, from his father, who said:\n\nI said, \O Messenger of ﷺ"," a man passes by me and does not offer me hospitality nor extend any generosity to me"," and then he passes by me [again] — should I repay him in kind?\"" He ﷺ said"," \""**No"," offer him hospitality.**\""\n\nHe said: \""And he ﷺ saw me wearing tattered garments and said"," 'Do you have any wealth?'\"" I said"," \""From every kind of wealth"," Allah has granted me camels and sheep.\"" He ﷺ said"," \""**Then let it be seen upon you.**\""\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā** (al-Tirmidhī) said: There are narrations on this topic from **ʿĀʾishah**"," **Jābir**"," and **Abū Hurayrah** (may Allah be pleased with them all).\n\nAnd this is a **ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ** hadith. **Abū al-Aḥwaṣ's** name is **ʿAwf ibn Mālik ibn Naḍalah al-Jushamī**.\n\nAnd the meaning of his ﷺ statement \""**aqrihi**\"" is \""**aḍifhu**\"" — that is"," \""offer him hospitality.\"" And **al-qirā** ("""
"2075","Aishah narrated from Wahb's daughter - and she is Judamah - who said:\I heard the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) saying: 'I wanted to prohibit Al-Ghilah"""
"2076","Aishah narrated from Judamah bint Wahb Al-Asadiyyah that she heard the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) saying:\I intended to prohibit Al-Ghilah until I remembered that the Persians and Romans do that"""
"2077","Qatadah narrated from Abu 'Abdullah that Zaid bin Arqam said:\The Prophet (S.A.W) would acclaim oil and Wars for (the treatment of) pleurisy.\"" Qatadah said: \""And it is put in the mouth on the side which he is suffering"""
"2078","Maimun Abu' Abdullah said:\I heard Zaid bin Arqam say: 'The Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) ordered us to use Qust Al-Bahri and oil to treat Pleurisy"""
"2079","Uthman bin Abi Al-'As narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) came to me while I had a pain that almost ruined me. So"""
"2080","Asma' bint 'Umais narrated that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) asked her what they used as a laxative. She said:\Shubrum\"" He said: \""It is hot and too strong.\"" She said:\""Then I used Senna as a laxative.\"" So the Prophet (S.A.W) said: \""If there was anything that would have a cure for death in it"""
"2081","Abu Sa'eed said:\A man came to the Prophet (S.A.W) and said: 'My brother is suffering from loose bowels.' He said: 'Let him drink Honey.' So he drank it. Then he came and said: O Messenger of Allah (S.A.W)! He has drunk honey"""
"2082","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Prophet (S.A.W) said:\There is no Muslim worshiper who visits one who is ill - other than at the time of death - and he says seven times: As'alullah Al-'Azeem Rabbal 'Arshil 'Azeem an yashfik ('I ask Allah the Magnificent"""
"2083","Thawban narrated that the Prophet (S.A.W) said:\When one of you suffers from fever - and indeed fever is a piece of the Fire - let him extinguish it with water. Let him stand in a flowing river facing the direction of it and say: Allahummashfi 'abdaka wa saddik Rasulak ('In the name off Allah. O Allah! Cure your slave and testify to Your Messenger.)' Doing so after Salat As-Subh(Fajr) and before the rising of the sun. Let him submerse himself in it three times"""
"2084","**Narrated by Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān**, who said: **Abū Dāwūd narrated to us**, who said: **Shuʿbah informed us**, from **Abū Isḥāq**, who said: I heard **Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Jadali** say:\n\n\I asked **ʿĀ'ishah** (may Allāh be pleased with her) about the character of the **Messenger of Allāh** (peace and blessings be upon him). She replied:\n\n'He was **neither obscene in speech** (*fāḥish*)"""","""" nor **one who sought to indulge in obscenity** (*mutafaḥḥish*)"""","""" nor **a loud clamourer in the marketplaces** (*ṣakhkhāb fī al-aswāq*). He did **not requite evil with evil**; rather"""","""" he would **pardon and forgive** (*yaʿfū wa yaṣfaḥ*).'\""""""""\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā** (al-Tirmidhī) said: *\""""""""This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.\""""""""*\n\n**Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Jadali's** name is **ʿAbd ibn ʿAbd**"""","""" and it is also said **ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd**.\n\n*This narration is recorded in Sunan al-Tirmidhī and is graded Ḥasan Ṣaḥīh. It beautifully encapsulates the noble moral character of the Prophet Muḥammad (peace and blessings be upon him)"""","""" highlighting his restraint"""","""" dignity"""","""" and magnanimity.*"""""""""
"2085","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said:\The parable of the ill when he is cured and becomes healthy is that of hail that falls from the heavens in its purity and its color"""
"2086","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said:\When one of you visits the ill"""
"2087","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet(S.A.W) visited a man who was ill"
"2088","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) said:\Whoever leaves wealth then it is for his heirs"""
"2089","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) said:\Learn the laws of inheritance and the Quran"""
